temperature

    1.  It's something that controls how much verify there is in the output that comes from th model.
        So it's the parameter that controls how different it would be each time you call it.
    2.  A temperature = 0; means it should be predictable and deterministic. The higher temperature means more varity,
        more difference in the answers each time you call it.
    3.  Some people says more temperature means more creativity. I don't this it's right.
    4.  What was it actually doing?
        a.  Its actually controlling at Inference time when we are generating token by token.
        b.  It's to do with how you pick which token comes next? A model or LLM doesn't predict a single next token.
            It predicts the probability of all possible next token every i.e every possible next token get
            some probability even it's a very small probability
        c.  Usually it picks the token that got the highest probability. One that the model says most likely next token.
        d.  With (temperature=0); All it does is to pick the token which got the highest probability and It pick that one
            token every single time. So, it's less random and more predicatable
        e.  with (higher temperature); we occasionally picks the tokens which didn't get the top probability, but may
            be the 2nd top or something like that.
    5. For Example:
        a. In case of OpenAI -> The temperature varies from 0 to 2
            > A temperature of 1 means
                > If a token gives a probability of 10% then we will pick that one 10 in 100 times
                > If a token get 1% probability; and it's really unlikely, still 1 in 100 times we might pick that one
                  if temperature is 1.
                > So there is more varity what comes out, but it doesn't means it's more creative. It means the word
                  choices would be different and sometime it might be bit odd when temperature is high enough. In fact
                  when the temperature=2; we can get quite strange answers.
    6.  2 Notes:
        a. We use words called deterministic and reproducible, but that's not quite right, because even with
           temperature 0, the output won't necessarily reproducible. Because there are random numbers involve running
           in LLMs.
        b. We can do something like setting a random c, which means those random numbers will be same each time.
           Even when we set random c it's still not guaranty to be same everytime, because there can be changes to
           frontier models, and also there are performance optimisation
        c. But If the temperature=0, and we set the random c; then we most likely get the same answer everytime.

    |

    As we see the temperature doesn't indicate the creativity. If we want out model to be more creative. The right way
    to do that is through system prompt. The right way to do that is through to instruct the model to be more creative.
    Give it example what it means to you to be creative, that's what creativity should be all about.

    If we want different answers, then the best way to do it is to tell it the previous answers and ask it to give
    different answers. That's the more reliable.


